the above gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2+1 & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the desired integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}(2f(x)-3)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x-3{\\int }_{-1}^{3}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-3\\cdot x\\,{|}_{-1}^{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-3(3-(-1)) \\\\  & =6-3(4) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078888 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d752aac-6187-595d-8818-b0179fd7380e" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Definite Integral Using Multiple Properties of Definite Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "860f25bd-cea8-5b65-b376-cb0913b54fe5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076540} {:answer/id #uuid "23dc41c5-4635-5f04-8757-c3e0bc36d0da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076541} {:answer/id #uuid "2829ac6b-de31-5329-a54f-3c1d21118d27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076542} {:answer/id #uuid "28ee6d01-c544-51ca-8a5d-f538b11903b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076543} {:answer/id #uuid "6c429e33-50a6-5edf-801e-c13bde0e78ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c429e33-50a6-5edf-801e-c13bde0e78ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076544} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae8b6523-1b19-5916-8ad4-bc753a22b74a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076539}] :question/id #uuid "77fb0fc1-711e-5505-92d1-e385391bf5f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-4798" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a function 